// An unsuffixed float literal a `float32` position types must fit `float32`, as an integer literal must fit its
// destination (`int8 a = 300;`). It was emitted as a C double and converted — undefined in C, `inf` in practice — and
// a compile-time one reached the C compiler as the undeclared name `inff`.
fn int32 main() {
    float32 x = 1e39;
    float32 y = 2.0;
    bool b = y < 1e39;
    return 0;
}
